From 4f25cc74e23bc8d1343e23ff75de84d7090ecd2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chaton <definitelyfrenchname@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 09:22:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] jtframe/sim: advance the model's own clock, so `#` delays
 fire under Verilator

`jtsim -verilator -stats` is inert at v1.7.3, for three independent reasons.
This commit fixes the one that lives in test.cpp.

hdl/ver/test.cpp keeps a private `simtime` counter and never calls
VerilatedContext::time(). VerilatedContext::time() therefore stays 0 for the
whole run -- and that is the clock $time reads and the clock the --timing
delay scheduler compares its deadlines against. So every `#` delay in the
design has a deadline that never arrives. The SDRAM usage reporter
(hdl/sdram/jtframe_sdram_stats_sim.v:112, and the identical construct in
hdl/sdram/jtframe_romrq_bcache.v:266) is an `initial forever #16_666_667`,
so it compiles, elaborates, and prints nothing.

Fixed by advancing the context clock alongside simtime, in JTSim::advance_time().
Naively assigning time()+=semi_period is NOT enough and was measured to abort
the run: a delay deadline lands wherever the design put it, not on the
half-period grid, and Verilator fatals with "Encountered process that
should've been resumed at an earlier simulation time. Missed a time slot?"
(verilated_timing.cpp:85). So the step lands on every pending time slot on
the way, using the model's own eventsPending()/nextTimeSlot(). eval() at an
intermediate time changes no input, hence creates no clock edge; it only
lets the delayed process resume.

semi_period is in picoseconds and the sim is built with
--timescale-override 1ns/1ps, so the arithmetic is exact. This is not gated:
it changes no DUT behaviour, and without --timing eventsPending() is always
false, so it costs one predictable branch per half cycle.

The other two reasons are caller-side and are handled in this project's
tools/run_sim_jtcps2.sh rather than here, since they are command-line
plumbing:
  * bin/jtsim:416-418 defines JTFRAME_SDRAM_STATS but nothing ever puts
    hdl/sdram/jtframe_sdram_stats_sim.v on the compile list, so
    game_test.v:380-392 instantiates a module Verilator cannot find;
  * Verilator 5 refuses `#` delays without --timing (%Error-NEEDTIMINGOPT),
    and --no-timing would compile the reporter into silence.

All three are upstream bugs rather than fork artifacts. Not filed as an
issue/PR from here.
---
 modules/jtframe/hdl/ver/test.cpp | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/jtframe/hdl/ver/test.cpp b/modules/jtframe/hdl/ver/test.cpp
index cec143d8c..ab4139636 100644
--- a/modules/jtframe/hdl/ver/test.cpp
+++ b/modules/jtframe/hdl/ver/test.cpp
@@ -453,6 +453,32 @@ class JTSim {
         }
     }
     void reset(int r);
+    // Keep the MODEL's clock in step with ours. simtime is a private counter;
+    // VerilatedContext::time() is what $time reads and what the --timing delay
+    // scheduler compares its deadlines against, and upstream never advances
+    // it -- so under Verilator every `#` delay in the design has a deadline
+    // that never arrives. That is why `jtsim -verilator -stats` reports
+    // nothing: the reporter in jtframe_sdram_stats_sim.v is an
+    // `initial forever #16_666_667`.
+    //
+    // A delay deadline lands wherever the design put it, NOT on our
+    // half-period grid, so stepping blindly by semi_period jumps over it and
+    // Verilator aborts with "Encountered process that should've been resumed
+    // at an earlier simulation time. Missed a time slot?" (measured). Land on
+    // each pending slot on the way. eval() at an intermediate time changes no
+    // input, so it creates no clock edge -- it only lets the delayed process
+    // resume. semi_period is in ps and the sim is built 1ns/1ps, so the
+    // arithmetic is exact; without --timing eventsPending() is always false
+    // and this costs one predictable branch per half cycle.
+    void advance_time() {
+        vluint64_t target = game.contextp()->time() + semi_period;
+        int guard = 1000; // a `#0` re-arming forever must not hang the sim
+        while( game.eventsPending() && game.nextTimeSlot() <= target && guard-- ) {
+            game.contextp()->time( game.nextTimeSlot() );
+            game.eval();
+        }
+        game.contextp()->time( target );
+    }
 public:
     int finish_time, finish_frame, totalh, totalw, activeh, activew;
     bool done() {
@@ -879,6 +905,7 @@ void JTSim::clock(int n) {
 #endif
         last_dwnd = cur_dwn;
         simtime += semi_period;
+        advance_time();
 #ifdef _DUMP
         if( tracer && dump_ok ) tracer->dump(simtime);
 #endif
@@ -890,6 +917,7 @@ void JTSim::clock(int n) {
         if( game.contextp()->gotFinish() ) return;
         sdram.update();
         simtime += semi_period;
+        advance_time();
         ticks++;
 
 #ifdef _DUMP
